  "final_message": "The event calendar is built: a Flask API with SQLite storage and a React/Tailwind frontend. I couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't available here. The UI also hasn't been tested in a browser, because the Chromium download for an automated browser test failed.\n\n**What I did check:** the frontend type-checks and builds after a clean `npm ci`. Six backend unit tests pass (`python -m unittest backend/tests/test_api.py`), covering sign-in, the 401s, create/read/update/delete, clearing omitted fields on `PUT`, validation, date ranges and sorting. I also ran the app under gunicorn and tried the main API calls with curl; the database file was created under the data directory.\n\n**Choices you may want to change:**\n- **End time:** an end time equal to the start time is allowed; only an end time *before* the start is rejected.\n- **Validation errors:** these return 400 with `{\"error\": ..., \"errors\": {field: message}}`. The create and edit forms show each message next to its field.\n- **Duplicate username:** registering a taken name returns 409.\n- **Date range:** `GET /api/events` returns events that overlap the range. A date-only `end_date` (e.g. `2026-11-09`) includes that whole day. It also accepts optional `limit`/`offset`, which you didn't ask for.\n- **Additions beyond the spec:** each event also returns `updated_at`. There are two extra endpoints, `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/auth/me`. Sign-in tokens are stored hashed and expire after 30 days.\n- **Times in the UI:** pickers use the browser's local time zone and send UTC to the API. Weeks start on Sunday.\n- **Extras in the frontend:** you can click an hour slot in week/day view to create an event there, and the arrow keys and t/m/w/d act as keyboard shortcuts.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- The Dockerfile now runs gunicorn with 2 workers and 4 threads.\n- `npm run build` now type-checks before building.\n- I added Tailwind and TypeScript, pinned their versions and updated `frontend/package-lock.json`.\n- I added `.gitignore`, a short Development section in `README.md` with the test and build commands, and excluded the tests and `.venv` from the Docker build context.\n\nThe main code is in `backend/app.py` and `frontend/src/` (`App.tsx`, `api.ts`, `dates.ts`, `components/`). Nothing has been committed.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
